# Key Metrics API Documentation

## Overview

The Key Metrics API enables retrieval of aggregated data metrics for companies, funding rounds, investors, and acquisitions. It supports single-level and two-level aggregation with customizable filters.

---

## Endpoints

- **Production:**  
    `POST https://platform.tracxn.com/api/3.0/companies/metric`


---

## Request Headers

| Header | Value | Required |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `accessToken` | \[Your Tracxn Access Token\] | Yes |
| `Content-Type` | `application/json` | Yes |

---

## Request Body Structure

### One-Level Aggregation

Use this to aggregate a metric over the entire filtered dataset.

``` json
{
  "filter": {
    "<filterName>": "<value>"
  },
  "metric": "<metricName>"
}

 ```

**Example:**

``` json
{
  "filter": {
    "practiceAreaId": ["5409cb72e4b0efef66413044"]
  },
  "metric": "sumFundingAmount"
}

 ```

---

### Two-Level Aggregation

Use this to aggregate and group metrics by a specified field.

``` json
{
  "filter": {
    "<filterName>": "<value>"
  },
  "metric": "<metricName>",
  "bucket": [{
    "field": "<aggregationKey>"
  }]
}

 ```

**Example:**

``` json
{
  "filter": {
    "practiceAreaId": ["5409cb72e4b0efef66413044"]
  },
  "metric": "sumFundingAmount",
  "bucket": [{
    "field": "country"
  }]
}

 ```

> _Note: Two-level aggregation returns results for only the top 20 categories._ 


---

## Available Metrics (Companies)

| Metric Name | Description | Example Use Case |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `sumFundingAmount` | Total funding amount | Calculate sector funding |
| `averageFundingAmount` | Average funding per company | Analyze funding trends |
| `medianFundingAmount` | Median funding value (ignores outliers) | Identify typical funding |
| `sumEmployeeCount` | Total number of employees | Measure workforce size |
| `averageEmployeeCount` | Average employees per company | Understand average company size |
| `medianEmployeeCount` | Median employees per company | Assess typical company size |
| `count` | Total number of entities | Count of matching companies |

---

## Available Filters

### Sector Filters

| Filter | Sample | Aggregation Allowed |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `practiceArea` | `practiceAreaId`: `["5409cf05e4b0831de3527d64"]` | Yes |
| `feedId` | `feedId`: `["538ca013e4b01fd726a7b617"]` | Yes |
| `businessModel` | `businessModel`: `["5b8e5eae4f0ca1fbcd668f14"]` | Yes |

### Location Filters

| Filter | Sample | Aggregation Allowed |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `country` | `["United States", "Israel"]` | Yes |
| `state` | `["California", "New York"]` | Yes |
| `city` | `["San Francisco", "Boston"]` | Yes |
| `continent` | `["Asia", "Europe"]` | Yes |

### Company Filters

| Filter | Sample | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `companyStage` | `["Seed", "Early-Stage Funded"]` | Early = Series A/B; Late = Series C+ |
| `foundedYear` | `[2008, 2009]` | Filter by incorporation year |

---

## Sample Requests & Responses

### One-Level Aggregation

**Request:**

``` json
{
  "filter": {
    "country": ["India"]
  },
  "metric": "averageFundingAmount"
}

 ```

**Response:**

``` json
{
  "result": {
    "result": 375321
  }
}

 ```

---

### Two-Level Aggregation

**Request:**

``` json
{
    "filter": {
        "practiceAreaId": [
            "5409cb72e4b0efef66413044"
        ]
    },
    "metric": "sumFundingAmount",
    "bucket": [
        {
            "field": "continent"
        }
    ]
}

 ```

**Response:**

``` json
{
    "result": [
        {
            "term": "North America",
            "value": 4.44963496937E11
        },
        {
            "term": "Europe",
            "value": 6.2989378232E10
        },
        {
            "term": "Asia",
            "value": 5.9903122715E10
        },
        {
            "term": "Australia",
            "value": 4.631035664E9
        },
        {
            "term": "South America",
            "value": 4.31366073E9
        },
        {
            "term": "Africa",
            "value": 2.898560734E9
        }
    ]
}

 ```

---

## Important Notes

1. Only top 20 buckets are returned in two-level aggregation.

2. All filters use AND logic by default.

3. Date values must follow `dd/mm/yyyy` format if applicable.

4. A valid `accessToken` is mandatory.

5. “Early-Stage” includes Series A/B, “Late-Stage” includes Series C and beyond.


---

# Companies API

### Fetching Detailed Company Profile

Once you have obtained the `id`, `name`, and `domain` from the Companies Search API, you can retrieve the full company profile using the **Companies Data API**.

- **Filter**: Only the `id` is required as a filter parameter.

- **Endpoint**: The endpoint remains the same as used for the search.

- **View Parameter**: To receive the complete company details, include the following in the request body: "`view:"companyData"`


---

## Request Details

### URL (Production)

`https://platform.tracxn.com/api/2.2/companies`

### Method

`POST`

### Headers

| Header | Value | Required |
| --- | --- | --- |
| accessToken | \[Access Token from Tracxn\] | Yes |
| Content-Type | application/json | Yes |

---

## Payload Body Parameters

| Key | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `filter` | Filters to apply (see filter section) |
| `view` | This is required to ensure you are calling the API to get the complete details of the particular company |

---

### Sample cURL Request

``` bash
curl --location 'https://platform.tracxn.com/api/2.2/companies' \
--header 'accessToken: [Your Access Token]' \
--header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
--data '{
  "view": "companyData",
    "filter": {
        "id": [
            "52bd669ce4b0ac0615891070"
        ]
    }
}'

 ```

## COMPANY FILTER

| FILTER | SAMPLE | NOTES |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **ID** | `id: ["nrG5itQu_3voVifgJjj52SGgucwK5dAJUNozT6vhxPw"]` | Company ID |

