# Companies API

### Fetching Detailed Company Profile

Once you have obtained the `id`, `name`, and `domain` from the Companies Search API, you can retrieve the full company profile using the **Companies Data API**.

- **Filter**: Only the `id` is required as a filter parameter.

- **Endpoint**: The endpoint remains the same as used for the search.

- **View Parameter**: To receive the complete company details, include the following in the request body: "`view:"companyData"`


---

## Request Details

### URL (Production)

`https://platform.tracxn.com/api/3.0/companies`

### Method

`POST`

### Headers

| Header | Value | Required |
| --- | --- | --- |
| accessToken | \[Access Token from Tracxn\] | Yes |
| Content-Type | application/json | Yes |

---

## Payload Body Parameters

| Key | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `filter` | Filters to apply (see filter section) |
| `view` | This is required to ensure you are calling the API to get the complete details of the particular company |

---

### Sample cURL Request

``` bash
curl --location 'https://platform.tracxn.com/api/2.2/companies' \
--header 'accessToken: [Your Access Token]' \
--header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
--data '{
  "view": "companyData",
    "filter": {
        "id": [
            "52bd669ce4b0ac0615891070"
        ]
    }
}'

 ```

